# Kaini — the poly keys from "Kaini Industries", fitted by measurement:
# one sawtooth through the ladder with the cutoff riding the keys note for
# note, so every register keeps the same round, dark colour (h2 a few dB
# under the fundamental, the fifth harmonic ~20 dB down). The filter env
# opens an octave at the strike and sinks over about a second, so a chord
# blooms and then goes woody while held. Organ gate on the amp, and the
# Juno's chorus II for the slow shimmer and the width (L/R correlation
# ~0.6, as measured on the track). Otherwise dry.
waveform 2
circuit 0
key_track 1
cutoff 640
resonance 0.65
drive 0.5
filter_env 1.05
filter_attack 0.01
filter_decay 1.0
filter_sustain 0
filter_release 0.1
attack 0.012
decay 1
sustain 1
release 0.1
chorus_mode 2
chorus_rate 0.5
chorus_depth 0.4
volume 0.849
octave 3
